    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;ve been trying to use rstan&#39;s pre-processor #include ability to share common functions among a variety of models, but the model isn&#39;t recognizing the functions when I run it in R.<br><br>A simple example:<br><br>toy_fun.stan:<br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// sqrt of a vector (elementwise)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector sqrt_vec</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">vector x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dims</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> res</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">m </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dims</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]){</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        res</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">m</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sqrt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">m</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">return</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> res</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">// other functions...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>toy.stan:<br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">functions</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#include</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;toy_fun.stan&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>transformed data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sX</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  sX </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sqrt_vec</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">// The rest of the model follows</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>These files are included in the same directory, which is also R&#39;s working directory.  Upon running the model:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rstan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>setwd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;~/R/ToyExample&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>n </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)^</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>toyFit </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;toy.stan&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> iter </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">400</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><br>I receive the following error message:<br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">SYNTAX ERROR</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> MESSAGE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">S</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> FROM PARSER</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">No</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> matches </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br><br>  sqrt_vec</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Function</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sqrt_vec </span><span style=\"color:#008\">not</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> found</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>ERROR at line </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">8</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    transformed data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">9</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sX</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      sX </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sqrt_vec</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                           </span><span style=\"color:#660\">^</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">11</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Error</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> stanc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">file </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> file</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model_code </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model_code</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model_name </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model_name</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>  failed to parse </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Stan</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;toy&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> due to the above error</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span></div></code></div><br>I have also tried a few variations in the #include statement, such as using the full path; none have worked.<br><br>Is there something I&#39;m missing?  I&#39;d really like to be able to use this feature. I&#39;m using rstan 2.9.0 on linux, and the same system had no difficulties compiling the rstanarm models.  <br></div>"
    ]
