     "<div dir=\"ltr\">On Sunday, January 24, 2016 at 3:10:28 PM UTC-5, Christopher Peterson wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;ve been trying to use rstan&#39;s pre-processor #include ability to share common functions among a variety of models, but the model isn&#39;t recognizing the functions when I run it in R.<br></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>You can&#39;t do it via stan(). You have to do something like this:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">sm </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> stan_model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stanc_ret </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> stanc_builder</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;toy.stan&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><code><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>toyFit </span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sampling</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></span></code></div></code></div><br>Ben<br><br><div dir=\"ltr\"><br></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
